  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759296,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1080° Avalanche: A GameCube Snowboarding Classic\n\n1080° Avalanche is a thrilling snowboarding game developed by Nintendo Software Technology and published by Nintendo for the GameCube, serving as a sequel to the acclaimed 1998 Nintendo 64 title, 1080° Snowboarding. Unlike many snowboarding games that prioritize tricks, Avalanche focuses on the adrenaline-pumping speed and precision of downhill racing. \n\nPlayers compete in various modes, including the signature Match Race, Trick Attack, Time Trial, and Gate challenges. A unique and perilous addition is the \"Avalanche\" – a daring run where players must outrun a rapidly approaching avalanche. With over 20 courses to master, the game supports both single-player and multiplayer experiences, including split-screen for up to four players and LAN connectivity.\n\nBeyond the core gameplay, Avalanche introduces unlockable boards for each rider, including surreal bonus boards like a penguin or a NES controller. Featuring visual output at 480p and Dolby Pro Logic II sound, the game offers an immersive and competitive snowboarding experience. A special edition, available exclusively at Walmart, included a bonus miniDVD with snowboarding and gameplay footage."
    },
